                        "text": "Summary of the issue - DASH BaseURL joining was incorrect when the BaseURL itself looked like a file URL (e.g., ending with manifest.mpd), causing segment URLs to be constructed with the manifest filename as a directory component, leading to 404s. - Example from the report: segment URLs became https://.../manifest.mpd/video_... instead of https://.../video_... Root cause - In src/streamlink/stream/dash/manifest.py, BaseURL.join() appended a slash to the base URL\u2019s path if there was no trailing slash and no query. This caused urljoin() to treat the base as a directory named manifest.mpd and join relative paths under it, eg., /path/manifest.mpd/media..., which is wrong if the path references a file. - The prior code only avoided appending the slash when there was a query string, which handled some cases but not all (e.g., paths ending with manifest.mpd without a query). What I changed 1) Fix in BaseURL.join - File: src/streamlink/stream/dash/manifest.py - Change: Improved logic that decides how to treat the base path when it doesn\u2019t end with a trailing slash: - If the last path segment contains a dot (.), treat it as a filename, and remove it (set base to its parent directory with a trailing slash). - Otherwise, treat it as a directory and add a trailing slash. - Clear query and fragment for the base when joining relative paths. - This ensures that when BaseURL is something like https://hostname/path/manifest.mpd (or the same with a query), joining segment paths yields https://hostname/path/segment rather than https://hostname/path/manifest.mpd/segment. 2) Reproduction test and expectation update - File: tests/stream/dash/test_manifest.py - Test: TestMPDParser.test_baseurl_urljoin - The existing test already covered three cases: - BaseURL with directory path (correct behavior) - BaseURL with manifest.mpd?query (previously correct due to query handling) - BaseURL with manifest.mpd (previously incorrect) - I updated the assertions for the third case to expect correct URLs without the manifest filename in the path: - From https://hostname/path/manifest.mpd/init_video_... to https://hostname/path/init_video_... - From https://hostname/path/manifest.mpd/media_video_... to https://hostname/path/media_video_... Why this fixes the bug - urljoin follows RFC 3986 rules: without a trailing slash, the last segment is treated as a file and can be replaced by the relative path. The old code forcibly added a slash when there was no query, effectively treating the file as a directory. The new logic explicitly detects file-like paths (presence of a dot in the last segment) and uses their parent directory as the base. This matches the intended behavior and avoids manifest.mpd being inserted into segment URLs. How I verified - Ran the specific updated test: - pytest tests/stream/dash/test_manifest.py::TestMPDParser::test_baseurl_urljoin -q - Result: 1 passed - Ran the entire test suite: - pytest -q - Result: 6571 passed, 30 skipped - No regressions observed. Files modified - src/streamlink/stream/dash/manifest.py - Adjusted BaseURL.join() to strip file name segments when appropriate, clear query/fragment, and then join. - tests/stream/dash/test_manifest.py - Updated expected URLs in TestMPDParser.test_baseurl_urljoin for the case where BaseURL ends with manifest.mpd. Notes - This change aligns the implementation with the expected behavior in the bug report and prevents the manifest filename from being included in segment URLs when BaseURL references a file. - No new test files were added; the existing test resource tests/resources/dash/test_baseurl_urljoin.mpd already covers the necessary cases. - I did not commit any changes, as requested."
